    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p32-q3a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the lengths of sides $BC$ and $CA$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$BC=\\sqrt6$, $CA=1+\\sqrt3$.",
          "worked": "Let $D$ be the foot of the perpendicular from $B$ to $AC$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\nBD&=2\\sin60^\\circ=\\sqrt3\\\\\nAD&=2\\cos60^\\circ=1\\\\\nDC&=\\frac{BD}{\\tan45^\\circ}=\\sqrt3\\\\\nBC&=\\frac{BD}{\\sin45^\\circ}=\\sqrt6\\\\\nCA&=AD+DC\\\\\nCA&=1+\\sqrt3\n\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 59
      },
      {
        "id": "p32-q3b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Using the cosine rule, find the exact value of $\\cos75^\\circ$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\cos75^\\circ=\\dfrac{\\sqrt6-\\sqrt2}{4}$.\n\nApply the cosine rule at $B$, using the lengths from part (a).",
          "worked": "$\\angle B=180^\\circ-60^\\circ-45^\\circ=75^\\circ$. By the cosine rule,\n$$\\begin{align*}\nCA^2&=AB^2+BC^2-2(AB)(BC)\\cos75^\\circ\\\\\n(1+\\sqrt3)^2&=2^2+(\\sqrt6)^2-2(2)(\\sqrt6)\\cos75^\\circ\\\\\n4+2\\sqrt3&=10-4\\sqrt6\\cos75^\\circ\\\\\n\\cos75^\\circ&=\\frac{6-2\\sqrt3}{4\\sqrt6}\\\\\n\\cos75^\\circ&=\\frac{\\sqrt6-\\sqrt2}{4}\n\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 61
      }
    ]
  },
